.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_DEVI_ENTER 9F
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_devi_enter ,
.Nm ndi_devi_exit ,
.Nm ndi_devi_tryenter
.Nd serialize changes to the children of a device node
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Ft "void"
.Fo ndi_devi_enter
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fc
.Ft "void"
.Fo ndi_devi_exit
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_devi_tryenter
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fc
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh PARAMETERS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va dip
Device node whose child configuration is to be serialized.
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
\fBndi_devi_enter()\fP enters the device-tree critical section associated with
\fBdip\fP, waiting if another thread owns it.
This serializes changes to the node's children, path information, and minor
nodes.
The same thread may enter recursively.
Each entry must be balanced by \fBndi_devi_exit()\fP on the same thread.
.Pp
\fBndi_devi_tryenter()\fP attempts the same entry without waiting for another
thread to leave the critical section.
A successful attempt, including a recursive entry, must be balanced by an exit.
.Pp
Acquire critical sections in order from ancestors towards descendants.
If an operation can enter the parent, enter the parent before the child.
Multipathing operations also require the virtual HCI critical section to be
entered before the corresponding physical HCI critical section.
Do not hold unrelated locks across calls that can invoke driver entry points.
.Pp
Entering \fBdip\fP protects its children; it does not acquire a reference to \fBdip\fP
itself.
Keep \fBdip\fP alive independently, for example through a device-node reference.
Use the parent's critical section when inspecting or changing a child.
\fBDEVI_BUSY_OWNED(dip)\fP may be used in assertions to check ownership.
.Sh CONTEXT
These functions may be called from user or kernel context.
\fBndi_devi_enter()\fP may block.
The try operation avoids waiting for critical-section ownership but is not a
high-level interrupt synchronization primitive.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
\fBndi_devi_tryenter()\fP returns 1 when it acquires the critical section
and 0 when it does not.
This is a boolean result, not an \fBNDI_SUCCESS\fP status.
The other functions have no return value.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ndi_devi_findchild 9F ,
.Xr ndi_hold_devi 9F ,
.Xr sunndi 9F
